  "starterCode": "# Attention Sinks — reconstructed educational contract\nimport numpy as np\n\ndef solution(scores, sink_count=1):\n    # TODO: implement the operation described in the problem statement\n    pass\n",
  "solution": "### 💡 Intuition & Approach\nThe implementation computes **Attention Sinks** by following direct architectural principles, leveraging vectorized operations to ensure both correctness and optimal runtime efficiency.\n\n### ⚡ Python Reference Implementation\n```python\nimport numpy as np\ndef solution(scores, sink_count=1):\n    # Add sink_count always-visible prefix positions; return a boolean visibility mask.\n    scores=np.asarray(scores); n=scores.shape[-1]\n    mask=np.tril(np.ones((n,n),dtype=bool))\n    if sink_count>0: mask[:,:min(sink_count,n)]=True\n    return mask.tolist()\n```\n\n### ⏱️ Complexity Analysis\n- **Time Complexity**: $\\mathcal{O}(N)$ where $N$ represents the primary sequence length or dimension.\n- **Space Complexity**: $\\mathcal{O}(N)$ auxiliary memory for computing and storing output representations.",
